Default theme font: DejaVu Sans, Bitstream Vera license and public-domain DejaVu changes.
See default-theme/FONT-LICENSE.txt in dialogue-presentation. The font is not relicensed under MIT.

The optional Minestom adapter includes an unchanged DejaVu Sans font source and
original generated glyph/skin assets. Font license and provenance are included
in each default-minecraft profile under assets/dialogue/font-source/.

The dialogue-minestom native glyph atlases and UI geometry are generated original
sample assets using the same licensed DejaVu Sans source. Each frozen profile
ships its source font and license under assets/dialogue/font-source and a verified
manifest. The optional post-effect shader is original project code. Minecraft
client metadata/bytecode was inspected locally for compatibility; no Minecraft
client code or texture files are redistributed.

The independent NPC dialogue example reuses the original neutral MIT example
model/clip/JSON from groundsgg/library-npc, by the same project owner. Its JSON
references vanilla texture identifiers without redistributing vanilla textures.

Native dialogue panel tiles reuse the original blue/gold pixel-frame painter
from the Grounds dialogue-java-probe preview (HudPackCompiler.pixelPanel).
They are original Grounds assets, not copied from Rivet or LuxDialogues.
The native encoder places precomposed, adjacent texture tiles instead of
overpainting coplanar border/fill glyphs. The maintenance generator retains
the preview palette and contour; the server never rasterizes these assets.

The compact HUD additionally reuses the original rounded modal and frozen
Monospaced glyph raster from the Grounds dialogue-java-probe preview. Source
pixels are retained under tools/prototype-hud; the generator pads bitmap cells
and uses native scaling without redrawing the source font. The font raster keeps
the bundled DejaVu/Bitstream license. No third-party server artwork is included.

Grounds panel palette overlays adapt the frozen dialogue-minestom 1.0.0 panel
atlases. Original stepped panel geometry is preserved. Only colors are changed:
normal border C1B9AA, selected border E7B84B, warm dark background.
The upstream artifact and individual imported assets are SHA-256 verified by
tools/import_dialogue_assets.py. DejaVu license remains in the complete bundle.

Guide speech samples and wordless greeting/farewell cues are original
AI-generated fictional vocalizations created
with ElevenLabs Sound Effects v3 through fal.ai on 2026-11-23. No franchise
recordings or imitated named character voices are included. See
the bundled Guide voice provenance for the source request and extraction details.
